  "summary": "A handwoven woolen textile from the Outer Hebrides islands of Scotland, known for its durability and distinctive flecked appearance.",
  "description": "Harris Tweed features a subtle, heathered texture from blending different colored wools, resulting in a mottled, flecked surface. Its production is protected by law, requiring hand-weaving in the weaver's own home in the Outer Hebrides, creating a textile deeply tied to Scottish heritage and craftsmanship.",
